From: Paul Slootman
Subject: Re: UDB traps

On Wed 18 Nov 1998, George A. Dowdingg wrote:

> While using dselect in ftp mode I get the folowing error(s):
> 
> identd(1897) unalligned trap at 0000015555556b845c: 000000011ffff95c 2d 10
> identd(1897) unalligned trap at 0000015555556b845c: 000000011ffff95c 2d 10
> 
> comments? ...

This is basically harmless, and not the fault of identd (as far as I
have been able to determine), but an optimizer(?) problem in fscanf of
libc.

It happens because you start an ftp session to a remote site, and that
site does an ident lookup to your machine to find out who is initiating
that ftp connection.

